scope: |
  RETRACTING MY OWN WRONG DIAGNOSIS, written into `v3/SPRINT.md` §SSC3-14b on 2026-08-13 and
  outstanding all of 2026-08-14 because the path was held by three claims in succession
  (`bench-b4-three-version-table`, then `v3-const-hoist`).

  The entry's last two paragraphs tell the next reader that the vararg star "is being eaten below
  the parser — in the lexer or in `alphabet/src/Alphabet.scala`" and that "the next step is a token
  dump, not another parser edit". The token dump was taken: `def total(xs: Int*)` lexes as
  `TId(Int) TOp(*) TPunct())` — the star is a live token at 1:18 and neither the lexer nor the
  alphabet touches it. The real cause is that `Front.default` is UNIML whenever `v3/.jars/uniml.cp`
  exists, so two attempts at `v3/src/Parser.scala` were measured through a front that does not
  compile the file; uniml discards the star at `ScalaSpike.skipTypeTail` (`ScalaSpike.scala:708`),
  deliberately and with a comment saying so.

  WHY THIS IS WORTH A CLAIM OF ITS OWN RATHER THAN A LINE IN THE NEXT ONE: the entry does not merely
  lack an update, it ACTIVELY MISDIRECTS — it names a file to go and read that has nothing to do
  with the defect, and it does so with the confidence of a measurement. SSC3-14b shipped in
  7bc7e2a1b hours ago, so a reader hitting that text now would be debugging a solved problem in the
  wrong subsystem.

  NARROW: one entry, two paragraphs replaced and the header marked done. No other SSC3 entry is
  touched; `range-replace-eats-neighbours-silently` says to anchor on the heading and check the
  neighbours survived, so the edit is anchored and the entry count is compared before and after.
  WIDENED IN SCOPE (not in paths) 2026-08-14 to the `## SSC3-14 — math` entry in the SAME file: its
  first line said "Measured 2026-08-13 and NOT started" for work that landed hours ago in a6a274571.
  That is the identical failure this claim exists to fix — a board entry stating something false
  with the authority of a measurement — and leaving it while correcting its neighbour would have
  been choosing which false line to care about. The original measurement is KEPT below the update,
  because the split it decided is still the record.

  VERIFIED, because `range-replace-eats-neighbours-silently` says a heading-anchored edit still has
  to prove the neighbours survived: entry count 72 before and 72 after, `## SSC3-14`/`## SSC3-15`
  and both earlier same-numbered entries still present, the old wrong text gone (grep count 0), all
  16 fences balanced, and `markdownlint v3/SPRINT.md` rc=0 — read WITHOUT a pipe, since piping a
  gate masks its exit code and the first run reported `head`'s status.
